Why: Under link-time optimization (CRAN's gcc LTO check) gfortran
 compares every call against the definition of the callee and warns
 (-Wlto-type-mismatch) when the argument types differ; 39 such sites
 remain after patches 0003-0007 (37 at first, 2 more once the others
 were fixed). Nine pass a Fortran string to C, whose hidden length
 gfortran >= 8 and flang pass as size_t while mumps_c_types.h declared
 it MUMPS_INT (int): the fallback definition of mumps_ftnlen is now
 size_t; the two binary dump routines called from dana_driver.F also
 get explicit interfaces, because for an implicit call gfortran types
 the hidden length of their file name as a signed integer. 28 pass data of one
 type to a routine declared with another because the callee only
 forwards the address (MUMPS_SIZE_C, MUMPS_ADDR_C, MUMPS_CHECKADDREQUAL,
 DMUMPS_ASSIGN_ROWSCA_LOC/COLSCA_LOC, the in-place 64-to-32-bit copies,
 the complex-domain mumps_flytes.c kernels, and the mixed-precision
 pack/unpack and solve kernels): they get explicit interfaces whose
 forwarded arguments are exempt from type, kind and rank checking, in
 the existing mumps_c_interfaces.h, the new mumps_flytes_interfaces.h,
 dmumps_f77.F, and the module specification parts of DMUMPS_BUF and
 DMUMPS_SOL_LR (the interfaces make the compilers check the actuals, so
 six elements of pointer or assumed-shape arrays at those calls became
 T4 rows). Two are wrong actuals: dsol_c.F calls DMUMPS_ROOT_SOLVE with
 19 arguments for 18 dummies (FROM_PP dropped) and
 dfac_process_blocfacto.F passes an INTEGER placeholder for the DOUBLE
 PRECISION M_ARRAY of DMUMPS_COMPRESS_CB_I (now a DOUBLE PRECISION
 placeholder).
Upstream: not sent; the ROOT_SOLVE argument count, the M_ARRAY
 placeholder and the mumps_ftnlen default are worth reporting.
Obsolete when: an LTO build (tools/README.md, conformance step 7) shows
 no -Wlto-type-mismatch warning without this patch.

diff --git a/include/mumps_c_types.h b/include/mumps_c_types.h
index 5bb9a08..403b149 100644
--- a/include/mumps_c_types.h
+++ b/include/mumps_c_types.h
@@ -54,7 +54,11 @@ typedef struct {double r,i;} mumps_double_complex;
 #ifndef mumps_ftnlen
 /* When passing a string, what is the type of the extra argument
  * passed by value ? */
-# define mumps_ftnlen MUMPS_INT
+/* rmumps: size_t, which is what gfortran >= 8 and LLVM flang pass
+ * (MUMPS_INT is the pre-GCC-8 convention and a type mismatch under
+ * LTO) */
+# include <stddef.h>
+# define mumps_ftnlen size_t
 #endif
 
 
